@* Nestor project detail *@
<link rel="stylesheet" href="@Url.Content("~/css/project.css")" />
<div class="project project-detail">
    <h2 class="detail-title">Nestor</h2>
    <partial name="_ProjectCarousel" model="@("nestor")" />
    <div class="detail-description">
        <div class="project-text">
            <p>In the spring of 2024 I took a class in Web programming (which I am currently a TA for). Nestor was a group project I completed with 3 other students using Django in Pycharm. The assignment was to create a job listings and applications website, both usable by employers looking for employees and employees looking for work. I was in charge of general structure and design of the site, as well as implementing the Virtual CV section and the application process. I remembered it being a lot sleeker looking than it actualy is, but for a first attempt, I think it's pretty good :)</p>
            <br>
            <p>I also designed the logo! Since this was a job applications website (exactly like Alfred.is), we decided to have fun and make a sillier version of their logo. Also, Alfred is known as Batman’s butler, but much more famously, TinTin's butler's name is Nestor. We like to have fun here.</p>
            <div class="project-logos">
                <img src="@Url.Content("~/images/Nestor-logo.png")" alt="Nestor logo" />
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <partial name="_ProjectGallery" model="@("nestor")" />
</div>
